Body:
I’ve fixed my issue. Here is the solution that worked for me:

- Change the `resource` name in`.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` from `https://app.example.com/mcp/` to `https://app.example.com/mcp` (remove the trailing slash)
- Add the new `resource` name to the`identifierUris` list in the MCP server app manifest.
- Create a new Entra ID application for public clients (e.g. OpenCode) with the PCKE flow enabled:
    -  Allow public client flows by setting `"isFallbackPublicClient": true`
    -  Add OpenCode redirect url "http://127.0.0.1:19876/mcp/oauth/callback" under "Mobile and desktop applications" (not "Web")
      ```
        "publicClient": {
		"redirectUris": [
			"http://127.0.0.1:19876/mcp/oauth/callback"
		]
	}
      ```

The final version of the MCP configuration
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "entra-mcp": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://app.example.com/mcp",
      "oauth": {
        "clientId": "<client_id_of_public_client_app>"
      }
    }
  }
}
```
